      <p class="ct-foot">Executed as a deed on a Tuesday. The witness confirms he was present at his own signing and had no notes.</p>

      <div class="addendum">
        <div class="ct-head"><span>Addendum</span><span>Opinion of US Counsel</span><span>Obtained after execution</span></div>
        <ol class="clauses" start="12">
          <li><b>It can be done there.</b> Following the impediment identified at clause 10, an opinion was sought as to whether the structure could be effected in the State of Delaware. It can. Section 160(c) of the <i>Delaware General Corporation Law</i> does not prohibit a corporation from holding shares in a corporation that holds it. It provides instead that such shares "shall neither be entitled to vote nor be counted for quorum purposes."</li>
          <li><b>Resulting position.</b> The structure therefore survives in Delaware in the following form: both entities exist, both are wholly owned, and none of the shares may vote. The company would be complete, solvent, properly constituted, and permanently unable to decide anything.</li>
          <li><b>Management response.</b> Management regards this as an improvement. Under clause 5 the boards were appointed without consultation. Under the Delaware arrangement no appointment is possible at all and the question does not arise.</li>
          <li><b>As to the register.</b> The United States required equivalent disclosure under the Corporate Transparency Act until March 2025, when an interim final rule redefined "reporting company" to mean entities formed under the law of a foreign country, thereby exempting domestic companies and approximately ninety-nine percent (99%) of the entities previously obliged to report. That rule has not been finalized. Accordingly the name appearing on the register at clause 11 appears nowhere.</li>
          <li><b>Instruction sought.</b> Counsel was asked whether this was the intended result of the legislation. Counsel replied that the question fell outside the scope of the retainer.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="ct-foot">This addendum is not incorporated into the deed. The period for incorporating addenda had closed (see clause 3).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
